<!--
    An expression over two halfwords of a stack local, read after a wider
    write that replaces one of them: P6 ActionMarkImplied, the
    Merge::inflateTest Cover check.  Source (gcc 11 -O0
    -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none):
        void swaphalves(unsigned long *input, unsigned long *output) {
          unsigned long state[4]; unsigned short t;
          state[0] = input[0] >> 7;
          state[1] = input[0] | (state[0] >> ((input[0] & 7) | 1));
          if (state[0] + state[1] == input[0]) {
            *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 0) = (unsigned short)input[0];
          } else {
            t = *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 2);
            *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 2) = *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 1);
            *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 1) = t;
            t = *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 3);
            *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 3) = *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 0);
            *((unsigned short *)&state[0] + 0) = t;
          }
          output[0] = (state[0] | state[1]) + state[1];
        }
    The high half of state[0] is rebuilt as CONCAT22 of halfwords 3 and 1
    after the write of the low half (halfwords 0 and 1) that replaces
    halfword 1.  ActionMarkImplied asks whether the CONCAT22 may be printed
    at its use, testing the pieces of state[0] that overlap halfword 1
    against the CONCAT22's live range, and read those pieces' Covers
    without rebuilding the stale ones, so the write between was missed:
    the printed C read ((unsigned short *)&v)[1] after the write that
    replaced it (wrong for every input taking the else branch whose
    halfwords 1 and 2 differ).  The Covers are now rebuilt before the
    test, so the CONCAT22 is saved before the write (#1) and the high half
    takes the saved value (#2, #3).
-->
